{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214884-campaign-setting-help-9-years-after-the-disappearence-of-the-scarlet-empress","id":1214884,"title":"Campaign Setting Help: 9 years after the disappearence of the Scarlet Empress","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-03T19:57:14-07:00","id":1214884,"title":"Campaign Setting Help: 9 years after the disappearence of the Scarlet Empress","content":"Hey all, I decided not to bog down the GM matchmaking thread because this is as much a Setting/Thought Experiment as anything else. <br /> <br /> I am getting ready to run a hearth of just graduated scions of the Scarlet Dynasty through many trials and tribulations, however I am in a bit of a quandary. The time frame that the game picks up is 9 years post disappearance of Her Redness, and so I am trying to figure out what other political/positional changes/drifts I should include about the state of the Realm.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I am seeing the Deliberative dissolving into power blocs centered around great house alliances along the lines people mapped out in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202437-mapping-great-house-politics\">this thread</a>. What I could see happening in the interim as a compromise to stave off a Civil War the Great Houses form an executive committee for administration of the Realm, with Amon Mora serving in a tie breaker capacity. However I am open to being challenged on this if you guys think that even 9 years post SE that there would still be no central authority. The one thing is that I want to ensure no CW starts yet, as a huge portion of the overarching story I am telling will be based upon that.<br /> <br /> What kinds of non-Civil War Setting changes do you guys see as reasonable for advancing the timeline a few years? Do you see any changes in the status quo happening within the 4 additional years or is that still too short a time horizon to see substantive changes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T02:23:00-07:00","id":1214975,"title":"","content":"Just brainstormning<br /> <br /> Big Changes<br /> 1) Continued Buildup and colonization: The Great Houses has continued to build up in an armsrace and conquest of the Threshold race. Venturing and conquering. Off to foreign lands.<br /> <br /> 2) The Blessed Isle has already fractured. In order to avoid civil war the Isle was carved into individual nations which belongs to The Great Houses or entirely new factions (like the Order or newly risen houses). Tensions between these new nations are still high. Espionage, checkpoints, papers please,<br /> <br /> 3) Solar kingdoms and Lunar invasions have grown so that they are now open and large. Seeing this threat the Realm decides to stand together and pur aside their differences for now. Although the internal conflict for who is commander in chief is still vicious and bloody. Under siege, intrigue, possible defection from the Realm.<br /> <br /> Might come up with some small changes in the future. Great thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T02:34:31-07:00","id":1214976,"title":"","content":"maybe a combination of light-hero's 1 &amp; 2. The Great Houses or faction try to improve their position by outright conquest of Threshold territories, but wind up sapping their power trying to hold them against Lunar, Solar, Undead, and Wyld incursions. No one is strong enough to make an overt move so outright civil war is put off. But things just get worse at home as administration degrades and succumbs more and more to corruption.<br /> <br /> <br /> or not. Maybe an unexpected alliance of two of the stronger factions could assert enough power to cower the others out of their moves. Or behind the scenes moves by Solsr PCs stabilize the situation (ever wonder what Manksque Cyan would be like as an Eclilse?). Or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T03:28:01-07:00","id":1214980,"title":"","content":"4) A divide across the isle (maybe a straight, maybe something close to). Two large factions of different houses split the isle both claiming to be the true Realm. Thinking a divide form North East to South West. This leaves each faction with primarily, similar divided satrapies. Of course you could draw the line differnetly. Maybe there where a short civil war (more like a few skirmishes and scandals or natural catastrophes) before this arrangement was made. Both sides for the Isle is antagonist towards each other. pull from themes from american civil war and korean civil war. Poor, but more free faction against rich, but tyrannical faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T04:36:42-07:00","id":1214992,"title":"","content":"Given the V'neef/Peleps situation I think any split will result in them being on different sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:27:13-07:00","id":1215035,"title":"","content":"If you go so far as to have the Blessed Isle formally divided into different nations (something that would be very hard to do without war) and have Solar and Lunar kingdoms encroaching, I think you would also start having the less pious houses start trying to tap into Anathema power through alliances.<br /> <br /> Maybe Peleps abandoned the Isle wholesale and took back or is fighting to take back the Caul as their new homeland, maybe V'neef is sabotaging them, or instead have them be consolidating themselves on the waters surrounding the Isle.<br /> <br /> Maybe even have Lookshy preparing an initiative to get a foothold on the Isle too. Or maybe they already got themselves a slice of the pie, and are themselves consolidating their gains on the Isle. Could be a part of the Peleps coup, offer Lookshy part of their Isle holds in exchange for holding the ground, to keep the Isle in turmoil as they pivot West.<br /> <br /> Not having a central authority would also spell chaos for the satrapy system. There would be a great deal of tribute knuckle dragging and rebellions are rolling in.<br /> <br /> Could be time for Mask of WInters to also move, maybe further inland, as to not provoke the Isle DBs.<br /> <br /> If the Scarlet Empire ceases to be, the whole of Creation is up for grabs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:40:42-07:00","id":1215045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214884-campaign-setting-help-9-years-after-the-disappearence-of-the-scarlet-empress?p=1214992#post1214992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the V'neef/Peleps situation I think any split will result in them being on different sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t want this to devolve SK far into Cold War power bloc. I considered doing a triple alliance with Ragara, Cynis, Sesus as one bloc; Mnemon, Peleps, and Ledaal another; with Nellens, Tepet, And Vneef forming a third, and Cathak alone given its military position...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T08:47:46-07:00","id":1215510,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that, at this point, no-one wants a war because they don\u2019t know how things will play out and they\u2019re not sure that they\u2019ll come out on top. Well, and the first person to move will get gang piled by everyone else.<br /> <br /> So, if after an additional 4 years of prep, they still haven\u2019t quite gotten ready, I think that works. There are likely going to be people chomping on the bit to just fight already, but it sounds like you\u2019re prepared for that. The situation you\u2019re describing honestly sounds a bit like Europe pre-WWI and you\u2019re just waiting for the Archduke to be assassinated, so going to look at some history from that period might be helpful.<br /> <br /> The main changes I foresee happening are that everyone\u2019s plans are progressing...but slower than they want. Enough Satrapies have broken away, crumbled, or \u201crequired military intervention\u201d to prevent anyone from amassing all the troops and funds they need and politics and red tape are complicating everything else.<br /> <br /> That said, the failure of House Tepet happened three years ago. Sudden upsets are a thing that happens.<br /> <br /> So, the takeaway here is...ask yourself \u201cwhat do you WANT to happen?\u201d and then justify it, because crazy things happen all the time. You want House Sesus and House Nellens to ally with each other? House Cathak implodes and all the mortal members jump ship to other houses? Ragara himself becomes the military Shogun of the Realm? Don\u2019t worry about how crazy it is, just say that it happens and figure out what crazy thing might have motivated it.<br /> <br /> Also, involve your players. If one of them wants to play a Nellens and one a Sesus, maybe they can tell you why the two houses are suddenly getting along. Maybe they all want to be from House V\u2019Neef and so you need to pay special attention to that House\u2019s status, but everyone else doesn\u2019t matter so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T10:55:50-07:00","id":1215548,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> Ok, I am a political science guy by background with a background in comparative politics. What I ideally want to show is the slow breakdown of elite consensus (the dragonblooded of the great houses) and power structures within the Realm, as Houses both are fighting against and preparing for the breakdown of the state. This would be a point of state regression, but only slightly, as the Houses still have not decided that they are better independent or to try and seize by force of arms YET. I absolutely am involving my players on this to the extent I sketched out the Major themes of the Chronicle and then let them assent to whether they would like to play in this space or not. I typically run with an Endpoint already in mind prior to even beginning the chronicle. The first 10-20 sessions however will be focused on the hearth, all scions from different houses who have just graduated secondary and are about to have their reunion before embarking on their Grand Tour (GT), having formed bonds of friendship during crucible of Primary. So far my hearth has:<br /> <br /> 1) A Mnemon Water-Aspected Immaculate monk who wants to persue a narrative arc similar to Preston in equilibrium.<br /> <br /> 2) A Tepet Earth-Aspect who is struggling against her own desires for isolation and a simple life and the weight of expectations of her House and her grandmother<br /> <br /> 3) A Nellens Wood-Aspect who sees the breakdown of the Realm coming, but doesnt know how to stop it or how to ensure that the there isnt significant loss of life in the process.<br /> <br /> 4) A Cynis-Fire Aspect who is disgusted with his own house and seeks to gain power to champion the poor and disenfranchised.<br /> <br /> I have one more player but he still hasnt fully decided on the concept he wishes to play.<br /> <br /> During the trek to essence 3, I plan on their GT to be serialized/episodic, visiting different areas and being young dragon-blooded, all the while the drumbeat of catastrophe begins to play louder and louder. I will admit, I'm heavily influenced in my narrative style by Babylon 5 and by the Mass Effect series, but my players all know this and I work on making sure they have sufficient space to tell their own personal stories within the larger narrative I plan on having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:35:36-07:00","id":1215830,"title":"","content":"The realm came together under a new charismatic leader, who charmed and bribed his way to the head...I don't know why something like The Iron Emperor jumped in my head when reading this XD. Some kind of authoritarian regime, that was created by the houses but has since reversed and they are now bowed to the throne, they now scramble for the scraps of power that they can. Rebellions flare on the periphery though, sparks of Solar energy igniting satrapies into rebellion, carving out kingdoms of their own.<br /> <br /> Endpoint may be something like deposing the Emperor, militarily, politically, or by any means necessary. No idea though.<br /> <br /> There's so many ideas for further down the line. Maybe the realm erupted in civil war and the Blessed Isle is a charred wreck as Essence was used to remove enemies from the land, dragon lines shaped and drawn their energy damaged. The rest of Creation had to watch as the realm tore itself apart accepting refugees from all numbers of houses. Some Houses still cling to their isle homes though, places of Sanctuary that the war didn't touch, and are attempting to heal the rifts.<br /> <br /> Sounds like from your own style though you will likely have a hub they return to, maybe a Manse/Vehicle they use for their adventuring as a base of operations for whatever they plan. <br /> <br /> Obviously there's likely to be all sorts of players in this game, abyssals, solars, lunars, dragon bloods, everyone trying to secure their own portion of the Isle.<br /> <br /> Honestly though it's what kind of stories you want to tell here as well, there's so many options ANYTHING could have happened, as long as you make exalted in scale and make your players feel like they're the heroes in the epic tale then everything will go well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}